#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119931 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119505 :question/id #uuid "1a6556a1-22b3-5e9b-97aa-d3e644df9f56" :question/math-academy-id "e-10993" :question/problem "Given that $\\det(A)=4,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\textrm{det}(A^T)=16$\n\n- $3\\textrm{det}(A^T)=12$\n\n- $\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)=17$" :question/worked-solution "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)=\\textrm{det}(A)=4\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Rather, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)=4 \\neq 16.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3\\textrm{det}(A^T)= 3 \\cdot 4 = 12.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A^T)+\\textrm{det}(I)= 4 + 1 = 5 \\neq 17.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6a3d254-c96f-5aa0-9db6-a587eb7cb2de" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050727 :topic/difficulty 1.0 :topic/id #uuid "6197c039-5830-56a2-b171-eac0f7516ad1" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059743} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059744} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059745}] :topic/math-academy-id 232 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048122} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049043} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049970} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050021} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050283} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050911} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050972}] :topic/title "The Transpose of a Matrix"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725787 :question-generator/id #uuid "3496a6fe-de49-5dbc-9437-efca4cc39726" :question-generator/script "generators/c2/c23cf82be4bce3c51b6f385db8ce2a8161521fd017a419aa9876cbf6e945b4df/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/