swer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704191}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85db6eb2-20ce-53e7-b285-2dadc1321933" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a square matrix with $\\det(B)=-3$, and let $I$ be the identity matrix of the same size.\n\nRecall that transposing a matrix leaves its determinant unchanged and that $\\det(I)=1$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Transposition preserves the determinant, and the identity matrix has determinant $1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(B^T)&=\\det(B)=-3 \\\\ \\det(I)&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $\\det(B^T)=-3$,\n\n$$\n\\det(B^T)=(-3)=-3.\n$$\n\nThis statement is **true**.\n\nFor $\\det(I)=1$,\n\n$$\n\\det(I)=(1)=1.\n$$\n\nThis statement is **true**.\n\nFor $\\det(B^T)+\\det(I)=0$,\n\n$$\n\\det(B^T)+\\det(I)=(-3)+(1)=-2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nThis statement is **false**.\n\nSelect $\\det(B^T)=-3$, $\\det(I)=1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a3bc34d-a4e8-524c-bfda-825cec3d05cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704175} {:answer/id #uuid "7713da0f-1a08-546b-9891-8e4644af6da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7713da0f-1a08-546b-9891-8e4644af6da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704190} :answer-field/id #uuid "01b47efe-7135-5cbb-aec5-40f896baab76" :answer-field/key "$\\det(B^T)-\\det(I)=-9$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52869827-7be4-505c-a4cd-a766e7f18803" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704183} {:answer/id #uuid "5897ccdf-cef2-5229-8695-afccf1b3625a" :answer/type {:db/ident :an